Backport of upstream QEMU 0f1d6606c28d (Mark Cave-Ayland, 2025-06-11):
  target/i386: fix TB exit logic in gen_movl_seg() when writing to SS
Fixes https://gitlab.com/qemu-project/qemu/-/issues/2987 — "QEMU TCG failed
to boot Windows 98 SE" (exception 0D on first boot after setup), a regression
from "target/i386: do not trigger IRQ shadow for LSS" which 9.2.4 carries.
Drop when we move to a QEMU release containing it (>= 10.1).

 target/i386/tcg/translate.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/target/i386/tcg/translate.c b/target/i386/tcg/translate.c
index 0fcddc2ec0885..0cb87d0201258 100644
--- a/target/i386/tcg/translate.c
+++ b/target/i386/tcg/translate.c
@@ -2033,8 +2033,11 @@ static void gen_movl_seg(DisasContext *s, X86Seg seg_reg, TCGv src, bool inhibit
         tcg_gen_trunc_tl_i32(sel, src);
         gen_helper_load_seg(tcg_env, tcg_constant_i32(seg_reg), sel);
 
-        /* For move to DS/ES/SS, the addseg or ss32 flags may change.  */
-        if (CODE32(s) && seg_reg < R_FS) {
+        /*
+         * For moves to SS, the SS32 flag may change. For CODE32 only, changes
+         * to SS, DS and ES may change the ADDSEG flags.
+         */
+        if (seg_reg == R_SS || (CODE32(s) && seg_reg < R_FS)) {
             s->base.is_jmp = DISAS_EOB_NEXT;
         }
     } else {
